        "narration": "Dana runs the 100 metre sprint. Her coach records each time in seconds. Today the stopwatch reads 12.45. How do we read that number?",
        "text": "12.45",
        "visual": { "kind": "emoji", "emoji": "⏱️", "count": null, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "The first digit after the dot counts tenths. The second digit counts hundredths. So 12.45 is 12 ones, 4 tenths, and 5 hundredths.",
        "text": "12.45 = 12 + 0.4 + 0.05",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "Money helps. A dollar splits into 10 dimes, and each dime is 1 tenth. Each dime is also 10 pennies, so 1 tenth equals 10 hundredths.",
